hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17132","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Asim al-Laythi narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Malik, and he was of his clan, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment, and I armed a man with a sword. He said: When he returned, he said: I never saw like what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, blamed us with. He said: Were you unable, when I sent a man and he did not carry out my order, to put in his place one who carries out my order."
"17133","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Bishr ibn Asim, he said: Uqbah ibn Malik al-Laythi narrated to us, he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was preaching, the speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, what he said was only seeking refuge from killing. Then he mentioned his story. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to him, displeasure known in his face. Then he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has refused me one who kills a believer. He said it three times."
"17134","Yunus narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, he said: A man joined me with Bishr ibn Asim, and he narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Malik, that a detachment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon the people of a water at dawn. A man of the people of the water came forth, and a man of the Muslims charged him, and he said: I am a Muslim, but he killed him. When they came, they informed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of that. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood addressing, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows, what is with a Muslim killing a man while he says: I am a Muslim? The man said: He only said it seeking refuge. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned his face away and extended his right hand and said: Allah has refused me one who kills a Muslim, three times."
